codemap 9
tour feature-show-help
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The human opens the window for the first time, or comes back to make a tour by hand and cannot find the next move. The goal is that understanding an unfamiliar codebase takes less friction here than in an editor with a language server, and the first friction is this window's own gestures. A first frame of this repo, shot before this tab existed, names none of ctrl+p, the arrow-key walk, or jump to definition. An empty map said the agent writes the tours, while + new tour is already in the Tours list. + step appears only while the pointer is on a symbol. A console note with spaces and no quotes is refused as extra arguments, seen when step-note was given the words builds and running. Typing help in the palette finds a file named help, and the console help command lists CLI commands. Nothing already in the window names the gestures. The Help tab sits beside the tour document. The first launch, when no layout has been saved, opens it beside the tour. The help button brings it back. The tab leads with making a tour by hand, then the console commands that path needs, then palette, jump, peek and back, then every other function of the window. Each line is that function's registry summary and its keys and gestures, so the tab cannot drift from the registry. A coach of seven lessons was built and dropped. It left the other functions unnamed and needed a second mapping from actions to features. A palette that opens already filtered to help was built and dropped. It has to be closed before the gesture can be tried, the palette caps the list, and those rows do nothing on enter.

